Instruction

Set this up on the backend so it can connect to the database.

Add a virtual environment:

cd backend
python -m venv venv

Then activate it and run:

pip install -r requirements.txt

Make sure you're inside the backend directory first; otherwise, this won't work.

Next, create a file named `.env` inside the backend folder.

Paste the contents that I sent in the group chat into the `.env` file (message me if you can't find it).

After that, test it by running:

python manage.py migrate

Make sure the virtual environment is activated. If everything works, you're ready to start.

To run and test the project:

Backend:

cd backend
venv\Scripts\activate
python manage.py runserver

Then open a new terminal:

cd ..
deactivate
cd frontend-mobile   (or frontend-web)

For frontend-mobile:

npm install
npx expo start

Then scan the QR code using your phone (install Expo Go from the Play Store), or use the URL shown in the terminal after running `npx expo start`.

For frontend-web:

npm install
npm run dev

Then simply open the local URL provided.

You'll need two terminals running at the same time—one for the backend and one for the frontend.

If you want to use a local database:

First, complete all the setup instructions above.

Create a database in XAMPP named:

mechconnect_se2

Then go to:

backend/.env

Read the comment for the `USE_SUPABASE` variable.

If `USE_SUPABASE` is set to `false`, run the migrations to create the tables in your local database:

python manage.py makemigrations
python manage.py migrate

Make sure you're inside the backend directory and that the virtual environment is activated before running these commands.

Complete the setup instructions above before doing this part.

For building the Android app:

eas build -p android --profile preview
